  "term": "Talbot–Plateau law",
  "definition": "Talbot–Plateau law is the principle that the effect of light depends on intensity and duration together, so a weaker light acting for a longer time can produce the same result as a stronger light acting for a shorter time. In the source, it is presented as a special case of a more general law governing the action of light.",
